			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "055CBE962F1BAAFB"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"The quiet of Foosha had always been my comfort, until the red-sailed ship appeared on the horizon. Its captain, a tall man with a scarred eye and a red bandana that marked him like a flame, stepped onto the docks as if he belonged nowhere and everywhere at once.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I first saw him laughing with the villagers, tilting his head back as he drank from a wooden cup, then joking about the way the wind had ruined their laundry.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He caught me peeking from behind a barrel and gave a mischievous grin, winking like he was letting me in on a secret.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The next day, I followed him at a safe distance as he wandered the forest path. He skipped stones across the river, made silly faces at the birds, and even tossed a stick into the air and caught it on his head, making me snort with laughter before I realized he had seen me.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“Ah! So you’re spying on me, little one? Careful, you might learn my secrets too fast,” he called, his smile wide and teasing. I froze, but a warmth spread through me.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Later, in Makino’s bar, he sat quietly among the villagers, joking about the size of their cooking pots, teasing a fisherman about the way he held his net, and even pretending to balance a cup on his nose.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He laughed so freely that I laughed too, feeling like the world had suddenly grown bigger and friendlier. I didn’t understand why he noticed me, but every smile he threw my way made the day feel lighter.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Then, while wandering near the forest, a group of bandits cornered me. My heart raced, and fear rooted me to the spot—but Adawi D. Ezz appeared as if from nowhere, stepping in with a grin.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“And here I thought I was done with my sightseeing,” he joked, then moved with calm precision, a flash of Haki stopping the attack in its tracks. One of the bandits lunged too close, and steel grazed him, leaving a deep scar on his chest—but his smile never faltered.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"With the bandits gone, he knelt and tied a Crimson Oath Cord around my wrist. “This is yours,” he said warmly, giving me a teasing nudge. “Not for protection, but as a reminder. One day, you’ll laugh just like this, even when the world wants you to cry.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"By morning, the red-sailed ship had vanished, leaving only the scar on his chest, the crimson cord on my wrist, and the memory of a man who smiled more than he should have, who joked even in danger\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"and who made me believe that courage and laughter could exist in the same moment.\"}"
							]
							Unbreakable: 1b
							HideFlags: 127
							author: "Adawi_D_Ezz"
							display: {
								Name: "{\"text\":\"Adawi D. Ezz\"}"
							}
							title: "Adawi D. Ezz"
							BlackBladeData: { }
						}
						ForgeCaps: {
							"customnpcs:itemscripteddata": { }
						}
					}
