			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "6663DBF7499ECC5B"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"I was seven the first time I met Yagus D. Boone.\\nBack then, the sea felt bigger than the world. Our village clung to it like it was afraid of being forgotten, wooden docks creaking under the sun, salt in the air every day of my life.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I was sitting at the edge of the pier, kicking my feet above the water, when the Marine ship arrived.\\nIt didn’t rush in. It didn’t warn anyone. It just appeared—white hull cutting through the waves like the sea itself had made room for it.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The Marines stepped off first. Straight backs. Quiet boots.\\nThen he did.\\nYagus D. Boone wore his coat loose over his shoulders, sleeves empty. A white Marine hat rested low on his head, clean despite the salt wind.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\" He looked relaxed, like nothing in the world could surprise him anymore.\\nI stared.\\nHe noticed.\\n“Kid,” he said, glancing down at me. “You gonna keep lookin’, or are you gonna say hi?”\\nI swallowed. “Hi, sir.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He smiled. Not wide. Not loud. Just enough.\\nThat was the first Marine I ever liked.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The pirates came that night.\\nNo flags. No warning. Just fire.\\nI woke up to screams and smoke. My mother shoved me toward the door, telling me to run. I ran until my lungs burned and my legs shook.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I fell near the docks.\\nA pirate loomed over me, blade glowing from the flames behind him.\\nI couldn’t move.\\nThen the dock cracked.\\nSomething heavy landed between us.\\nThe heat vanished.\\nI looked up.\\nVice Admiral Boone stood there.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He didn’t shout. He didn’t rush.\\nHis body shifted—slow, deliberate. Scales rolled across his skin like living armor. Massive plates rose along his back, sharp and uneven. A thick tail dragged behind him, crushing wood without effort.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"A Stegosaurus.\\nI felt small. Safer than I’d ever felt in my life.\\nOne pirate laughed and threw a burning chain.\\nBoone turned.\\nHe stepped in front of me.\\nThe fire exploded against his face.\\nI screamed.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The flames faded, leaving a deep burn carved around his eye, skin blackened and angry.\\nHe didn’t flinch.\\nDidn’t even blink.\\nHe exhaled slowly, smoke curling from his mouth.\\n“My fault,” he said calmly. “Stood a bit too close.”\\nThen he moved.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The world shook. His tail swept the dock clean. His plates smashed through steel and bone like they were nothing. Pirates flew. Ships broke. The night ended.\\nWhen it was over, he stood there, back straight, blood drying on his face.\\nI tugged on his coat.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“Doesn’t it hurt?” I asked, my voice shaking.\\nHe looked down at me.\\n“Yeah,” he said. “But pain passes.”\\n“What doesn’t?” I asked.\\nHe smiled.\\n“Regret.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The morning after, the fires were gone.\\nThe Marines prepared to leave.\\nI ran to the dock before I could think better of it.\\n“I’m gonna be a Marine!” I shouted.\\nBoone turned.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He walked back to me and crouched—not weak, not tired, just to meet my eyes.\\n“Why?” he asked.\\n“So I can stand in front of people,” I said. “So no one gets burned instead of me.”\\nFor a moment, he studied me like I was something important.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Then he took off his Marine hat.\\nHe placed it gently on my head. It was too big. It slid down over my eyes.\\n“Then start by carryin’ that,” he said. “Strength comes later.”\\nI grabbed the brim with both hands.\\n“I won’t lose it,” I said.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He stood and turned toward his ship.\\nAs it sailed away, the wind tried to steal the hat from me.\\nIt didn’t succeed.\\nAnd from that day on, whenever the sea looks too big, I remember the man who never stepped back—and I know exactly what I want to become.\\n\"}"
							]
							HideFlags: 127
							author: "Adawi_D_Ezz"
							display: {
								Name: "{\"text\":\"Yagus D. Boone\"}"
							}
							title: "雅格斯·D·布恩"
							BlackBladeData: { }
						}
					}
				}
				{
					id: "6DC021370DE32755"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "cartaddon:marine_fit_hat"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							GradeData: {
								ReappraiseUsed: 0b
