							{
								lvl: 5s
								id: "minecraft:thorns"
							}
						]
						display: {
							Name: "{\"text\":\"§e§lHunter Mace - Blitz D. Noah's Cape\"}"
						}
						Damage: 0
						BlackBladeData: { }
					}
				}
				secret: true
				nbt: {
					ForgeCaps: {
						"mineminenomi:entity_stats": {
							faction: "mineminenomi:bounty_hunter"
						}
					}
				}
			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "34430806036846BE"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"I was small enough that the rain felt heavier back then.\\nEach drop hit my shoulders like it meant to knock me flat. My shoes were full of water. My hands were numb. I remember thinking that if I stopped running, even for a second, the road would swallow me.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Then I heard the horse.\\nIt wasn’t fast. That’s what scared me. Whatever was coming didn’t need to rush.\\nThe rider slowed when he saw me. The horse snorted, steam rolling from its nose.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The man on its back wore armor darker than the sky, and a dark blue cape that moved like it had a mind of its own. A mace rested against his leg, heavy enough that I wondered how he carried it so easily.\\nHe looked down at me.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“…You’re shaking,” he said.\\n“I’m fine,” I lied.\\nHe studied me like a problem he’d already solved.\\n “No,” he said. “You’re alive. That’s different.”\\nHe dismounted, boots sinking into the mud. Up close, he was bigger than I thought. \"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Wider. Solid in a way that made the world feel smaller around him.\\n“What’s your name?” he asked.\\nI opened my mouth. Nothing came out.\\n “…I don’t use it anymore.”\\nHe nodded once.\\n “Good,” he said. “Names make people easy to find.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"A sound came from the trees. Metal scraping. Voices.\\nThe man’s hand dropped to his mace.\\n“Stand behind me,” he said. Not loud. Not sharp. Like he was asking me to step out of the rain.\\n“I can help,” I said, even though my legs were shaking.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He glanced back at me. His eyes were calm. Almost bored.\\n “Kid,” he said, “you already are.”\\nHe stepped forward.\\n“Blitz D. Noah,” he said, rolling his shoulders. “Hunter Mace.”\\nThen the road exploded into motion.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He moved like the weight of the mace didn’t exist. Every swing was clean. Final. I watched men fly like they’d been hit by a wall. The rain didn’t slow him. The mud didn’t take his footing.\\nOne of them rushed me.\\nI saw the blade. I froze.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Noah was there instantly.\\nHe shoved me aside—and something snapped.\\nThe sound was wrong. Too loud. Too final.\\nA metal trap clamped down on his leg.\\nI screamed.\\nNoah didn’t.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He looked down at it. Just… looked. Then he bent, pried the jaws apart with his bare hands, and pulled himself free. Blood soaked into the mud, dark and thick.\\n“That’s inconvenient,” he said.\\nI stared at him. “Y-your leg—”\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He tested his weight. The bone bent where it shouldn’t. He didn’t even flinch.\\n“They’ll think this stops me,” he said. “That’s their mistake.”\\nThe last of them ran.\\nWhen it was over, Noah sat on a rock like he was just tired, not broken. \"}"
								"{\"text\":\" He tore a strip from his sleeve and wrapped his leg tight. His hands didn’t shake.\\nMine wouldn’t stop.\\n“I’m sorry,” I whispered. “If I hadn’t been there—”\\nHe looked at me then. Really looked.\\n“Don’t ever say that again,” he said.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"His voice wasn’t angry. It was absolute.\\n“I chose,” he continued. “That’s all there is to it. Limbs grow back in other ways.”\\nI didn’t understand. I still don’t think I do.\\nAfter a moment, he reached up and unclasped his dark blue cape.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\" The rain had finally stopped, and for a second the fabric caught the light like the night sky.\\nHe placed it over my shoulders.\\nIt was heavy. Warm. It smelled like steel and road dust.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“Take it,” he said. “You’ll need something to remind you that fear doesn’t get the last word.”\\nI shook my head. “What about you?”\\nHe smiled. Not wide. Not sad. Just certain.\\n “I’ve got enough stories already.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I held the cape with both hands.\\n “I’ll remember you,” I said.\\n“I know,” Noah replied. “You’re still here.”\\nWhen I walked away, I didn’t look back.\\nI was afraid if I did, I’d see him standing tall—one leg, no regrets—and I wouldn’t be able to leave.\\n\"}"
							]
							HideFlags: 127
							author: "Adawi_D_Ezz"
							display: {
								Name: "{\"text\":\"Blitz D. Noah\"}"
							}
							title: "闪电 D. 诺亚"
							BlackBladeData: { }
						}
					}
				}
