				secret: true
				nbt: {
					ForgeCaps: {
						"mineminenomi:entity_stats": {
							faction: "mineminenomi:revolutionary"
						}
					}
				}
			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "656A239FA0EF10A3"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"I was hiding, even if I didn’t want to admit it.\\nThe alley was cold and wet, and my back hurt from the stones. I held a piece of bread in my hand, but I wasn’t hungry anymore. Every sound felt too loud. Water dripping. My own breathing.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Then someone spoke.\\n“You’re bad at hiding.”\\nI jumped so hard my head hit the wall.\\nA man stood at the end of the alley. He was tall—taller than anyone I knew. He had a saber on his hip, and the handle looked old, like it had been held forever.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\" Around his waist was a black cloth, tied in a loose knot. It moved when the wind passed, like it was alive.\\n“I—I’m not hiding,” I said.\\nHe looked at me for a moment. Not angry. Just… sharp. Like he was measuring the world.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“Then you chose a bad place to rest,” he said.\\nI heard boots. More than one pair. They were close.\\nThe man noticed too. His hand moved, slow, to the saber. He stepped in front of me without asking.\\n“What’s your name?” he asked.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I swallowed. “I don’t have one.”\\nHe didn’t argue. “Alright. Then listen. When I tell you to run, you run.”\\n“Why?” I asked.\\nHe smiled a little. It wasn’t a happy smile.\\n“Because they’re not here for me.”\\nThe boots stopped at the alley’s mouth.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“Found them,” someone said.\\nMy heart started beating so fast it hurt. I didn’t think. I grabbed the man’s coat.\\n“I’m sorry,” I whispered. “I didn’t mean to—”\\n“Let go,” he said, still calm.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"But I didn’t. My hands wouldn’t move.\\nThey rushed him.\\nSteel flashed. The saber sang when it left its sheath. He moved fast—faster than I thought anyone could. One man fell. Then another. The alley filled with shouting and metal and rain.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I should’ve run.\\nI didn’t.\\nSomeone came from the side. I saw it too late. A blade, swinging toward me.\\nI screamed.\\nThe man turned.\\nHe stepped between us.\\nPain sounded like tearing cloth.\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He didn’t shout. He didn’t fall right away. He just looked down, confused, like his body had betrayed him. His left arm was gone below the shoulder, blood spilling dark and fast onto the stones.\\n“No,” I said. “No, no, no—this is my fault.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He dropped to one knee. Still holding the saber in his right hand.\\n“Hey,” he said. His voice was rough now. “Look at me.”\\nI did.\\n“You’re alive,” he said. “That’s what matters.”\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"The others ran. I don’t remember when. The alley went quiet again, except for the rain and my crying.\\nI pressed my hands to the wound, shaking. “I didn’t run. I was scared.”\\n“I know,” he said. “So was I, once.”\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"He untied the black cloth from his waist with one hand. It was warm when he wrapped it around me. Too big. It smelled like steel and smoke.\\n“Keep this,” he said. “So you remember.”\\n“Remember what?” I asked.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"“That someone chose you,” he said. “And that you’ll choose others someday.”\\nI didn’t want to take it. My hands were covered in his blood.\\n“Train,” he said softly. “Get strong. If you want to stand where I stood… then earn it.”\\nHis eyes closed.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"I sat there until people came.\\nI kept the cloth.\\nThat’s when I decided.\\nI would grow strong enough to never freeze again.\\n Strong enough to stand in front of someone else.\\nStrong enough to join the Revolutionary Army.\\n\"}"
							]
